* Component Created by Javier Petrucci and Agustin Gullino
* jpetrucc@itba.edu.ar / agullino@itba.edu.ar
*
* Phase comparator type 3 (PC3 of the 74HCT4046A): edge-triggered set-reset flip-flop.
* Vo goes to Vcc on the rising edge of Vi and to 0 on the rising edge of Vf (threshold Vcc/2,
* all referred to ground). Levels do not matter, only rising edges: average Vo = Vcc*phi/(2*pi),
* phi = phase of Vf behind Vi (0 to 360 deg).
* Ideal model, not the internal circuit: everything is XSPICE digital (event driven), so it adds
* no analog equations besides the output bridge.
.SUBCKT Phase_Comp_Type3 Vi Vf Vo PARAMS: Vcc=5

* inputs to digital: Schmitt with 20 mV of hysteresis around Vcc/2 (only 0 or 1, never unknown)
Ain [Vi Vf] [vi_d vf_d] pc3_in
Aone one pc3_one
* Q: set on the rising edge of Vi (D=1), cleared by rst
Aq one vi_d null rst q nq pc3_ff
* rst: pulse on the rising edge of Vf while Q is high (held cleared while Q is low)
Ar one vf_d null nq rst null pc3_ff
Aout [q] [Vo] pc3_out

.model pc3_in adc_bridge(in_low={Vcc/2+10m} in_high={Vcc/2-10m})
.model pc3_one d_pullup
.model pc3_ff d_dff(clk_delay=1e-12 set_delay=1e-12 reset_delay=1e-12 rise_delay=1e-12 fall_delay=1e-12)
.model pc3_out dac_bridge(out_low=0 out_high={Vcc} out_undef={Vcc/2} t_rise=1n t_fall=1n)

.ends Phase_Comp_Type3
